<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p39_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is organized with the chemical structure of T4 at the top left, labeled as \"3,5,3',5'-Tetraiodothyronine (thyroxine, T4).\" Arrows extend from T4 to two pathways: one labeled \"Activation\" leading to T3 and another labeled \"Inactivation\" leading to reverse T3. Below the activation pathway, the chemical structure of T3 is shown with the label \"3,5,3'-Triiodothyronine (T3),\" and an arrow points from T3 to \"Inactivation\" leading to 3,3'-diiodothyronine. On the right, the structure of reverse T3 is positioned with the label \"3,3',5'-Triiodothyronine (reverse T3),\" and an arrow also points from reverse T3 to \"Inactivation\" leading to 3,3'-diiodothyronine. At the bottom, the chemical structure of 3,3'-diiodothyronine is displayed with its label." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
