<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p54_b11> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image centers on the thyroid gland, shown in a cross-sectional view with the label \"Thyroid\" directly beneath it. Blue lines extend from the thyroid to several other organs, indicating their interconnectedness. The brain is positioned to the upper right, the heart to the lower right, and the kidneys further to the right of the heart. The intestines are located to the left of the thyroid, with the liver placed to the left of the intestines. The female reproductive system is at the bottom left. Each organ is depicted in a detailed, three-dimensional view. The text \"Can Spread Effects\" appears in the top-left corner, while \"Abnormalities\" is written in the bottom-left corner." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
