<http://snomed.info/id/116154003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Patients" <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p26_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "At the top of the image, a section labeled \"capillary\" is connected to a \"cell\" with an arrow. Inside the cell, a blue box labeled \"deiodinase\" is positioned near components labeled \"MIT\" in orange and \"DIT\" in yellow, alongside blue boxes labeled \"T3\" and \"T4.\" The pathway starts with iodine (I-) entering the cell through a channel labeled \"(i).\" Below the deiodinase section, a box labeled \"protease peptidase\" is connected to \"thyroglobulin synthesis.\" On the right, three circles labeled \"colloid drops\" each contain small blue boxes representing T3 and T4 hormones. A section labeled \"peroxidase\" is present, producing hydrogen peroxide (H2O2), used in forming MIT and DIT from thyroglobulin. The bottom part of the image shows a wavy line labeled \"colloid,\" containing MIT and DIT thyroglobulin complexes, with arrows indicating their movement towards peroxidase and the formation of T3 and T4 hormones. Various arrows connect different parts of the diagram, showing the flow of substances and processes involved in thyroid hormone synthesis." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
