<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p9_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a cross-section of a thyroid follicle. At the center is a large, circular region filled with a pinkish substance, labeled as \"Colloid.\" Surrounding this colloid are oval-shaped follicular cells, forming a single layer. The follicular cells are positioned at the top left and bottom right corners of the image, with nuclei featuring prominent nucleoli. At the bottom left corner, a thin, elongated structure labeled \"Capillary\" is shown, containing red blood cells, indicating it is a blood vessel. Adjacent to the capillary, at the bottom right, are the parafollicular cells, also oval-shaped with similar nuclei, situated between the capillary and the follicular cells. The layout clearly illustrates the follicular cells encircling the colloid, with parafollicular cells positioned between the follicular cells and the capillary." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
