<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p15_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image is divided into two sections. On the left, a cross-sectional view of a thyroid follicle is shown, with multiple gray cells arranged in a circular pattern around a central pinkish-purple area labeled \"Colloid.\" Yellow dots, representing Na/I symporters, are scattered along the outer edges, and the follicle's boundary is outlined with a dashed black line. On the right, a detailed explanation of ion movement is provided. At the top, labels for \"Iodide ion\" and \"Sodium ion\" are present. A yellow cell is depicted with arrows showing the movement of ions: red arrows indicate movement from the extracellular space to the colloid, labeled \"Out of cell into colloid,\" while blue arrows point from the extracellular space into the cell, labeled \"Out of cell via Na pumps.\" The right side includes text explaining that high extracellular Na+ maintains low intracellular Na+, aided by sodium pumps." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
