<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p32_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram places the hypothalamus at the top as a yellow, rounded structure with a darker interior. Below it, the pituitary is depicted as a blue, teardrop-shaped structure. A red arrow labeled \"TRH STIMULATION\" connects the hypothalamus to the pituitary, while another red arrow labeled \"INHIBITION\" points back from the pituitary to the hypothalamus. Further down, the liver is shown as a pink, irregularly shaped structure, with a label pointing to it indicating thyroid binding proteins. The thyroid gland is positioned below the liver, appearing as a pink, butterfly-shaped structure. A red arrow labeled \"TSH STIMULATION\" extends from the liver to the thyroid. A black circle containing the labels \"T4\" and \"T3\" is connected by red arrows to the thyroid gland. Additionally, a black oval labeled \"Free Hormone\" is connected by an arrow to another black oval labeled \"Bound Hormone.\"" <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
