<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p23_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is divided into three sections. The top section has a pink background with the label \"Colloid\" at the top right corner. Below this label, several blue and yellow structures, resembling molecules or proteins, are present, labeled as \"iodinated thyroglobulin\" on the left side. The middle section has a gray background representing the interior of a cell. At the top, the word \"endocytosis\" is written in black text. Below this, there is a green oval labeled \"lysosome.\" To the right of the lysosome, a smaller purple circle contains a structure similar to those in the colloid section, with an arrow pointing from this circle to the green oval. Below the green oval, another green oval filled with blue and yellow dots represents the breakdown of iodinated thyroglobulin. The bottom section has a pink background labeled \"Extracellular fluid (into blood)\" at the bottom right corner. Several yellow dots, representing iodine ions, are scattered across this section." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
