<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p37_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram features a large purple circle labeled \"Thyroglobulin\" at the top left corner. An arrow points from this circle to a yellow region labeled \"Exocytosis,\" indicating the release of thyroglobulin into the colloid. Near this arrow is a yellow circle with a red dot, labeled \"Tyrosyl residue.\" A green oval labeled \"Iodination\" is connected by an arrow to the tyrosyl residue, showing the addition of iodine. Another green oval labeled \"Peroxidase\" is connected to the iodination step, highlighting the enzyme's role. A green oval labeled \"Follicle cell\" is connected by an arrow to the peroxidase, representing the cellular environment. A green arrow points from the follicle cell to the thyroglobulin, indicating TSH stimulation. Another green arrow, labeled \"Endocytosis,\" points from the thyroglobulin back to the follicle cell, showing reuptake. On the right side, a yellow region labeled \"Colloid\" contains iodinated tyrosyl residues. Within the colloid, a yellow circle with two red dots is labeled \"Diiiodotyrosyl residue (DIT),\" and another yellow circle with one red dot is labeled \"Monoiodotyrosyl residue (MIT).\"" <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
