<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p21_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with \"Blood\" at the top left corner and \"Follicle\" at the top right. A red arrow connects \"Blood\" to \"Follicle,\" indicating iodine's entry. Inside the follicle, a black arrow points from \"Iodine\" to \"Peroxidase,\" showing peroxidase's action on iodine. Another red arrow leads from \"Peroxidase\" to \"Enzyme-I,\" indicating enzyme production. This is followed by a red arrow from \"Enzyme-I\" to \"Iodinated thyroglobulin,\" showing its formation. Another red arrow points from \"Iodinated thyroglobulin\" to \"Thyroglobulin-I thyroxine-triiodothyronine,\" indicating conversion. A subsequent red arrow leads from \"Thyroglobulin-I thyroxine-triiodothyronine\" to \"Lysosomal proteases,\" suggesting enzymatic breakdown. Finally, a red arrow goes from \"Lysosomal proteases\" to \"Thyroxine Triiodothyronine,\" showing hormone release, and a black arrow points back to the follicle, indicating pinocytosis." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
