<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p49_b2> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with TSH positioned at the top left, represented as a red, curved shape, and an arrow pointing towards the receptor antibody on the cell membrane. The receptor antibody is near the top right, shown as a red, fork-like shape extending into the cell membrane. The cell membrane itself is a large, curved beige shape at the bottom of the image. Within this membrane, the TSH receptor is depicted as a red, rectangular shape with a smaller red shape inside it. A pink, irregularly shaped structure, the regulatory protein, is also within the cell membrane and connected to the TSH receptor by arrows. Adenylate cyclase is a purple, diamond-shaped structure connected to the regulatory protein, while cyclic AMP is a yellow, rectangular shape connected to adenylate cyclase. ATP is a brown, rectangular shape at the bottom right, connected to cyclic AMP, and GTP is a blue, rectangular shape at the bottom left, connected to the regulatory protein. GDP is a light blue, rectangular shape below the GTP, also connected to the regulatory protein. A light green, rectangular shape at the bottom center is connected to the regulatory protein as well. Arrows throughout the diagram indicate the flow of substances and interactions between components." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
<http://snomed.info/id/3716002> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#mentionCount> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
