<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p48_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A large oval encompasses the entire diagram, with a small box labeled \"T₃\" situated in the upper left corner, connected by a dashed line to the center. Within the oval, a rectangular box labeled \"T₃\" directs an arrow to a smaller box labeled \"TR,\" signifying the Thyroid Receptor. Below the \"TR\" box, a wavy line labeled \"TRE\" represents a specific DNA sequence. To the right of the \"TRE,\" a larger rectangle labeled \"α2\" connects to a smaller rectangle labeled \"mRNA\" via a wavy line. An arrow from the \"mRNA\" box points to another box labeled \"Pol II,\" which in turn directs an arrow to a curved line labeled \"T₃-responsive gene.\" Finally, an arrow from the \"T₃-responsive gene\" box leads to a box labeled \"Protein,\" with three listed effects below: \"Differentiation,\" \"Metabolism,\" and \"Other effects of T₃.\"" <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
