<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p33_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the hypothalamus at the top, depicted as a purple structure with a yellow circle labeled \"TRH.\" Below it is the anterior pituitary gland, shown as a pink structure with a yellow circle labeled \"TSH.\" The thyroid gland is positioned beneath the anterior pituitary, illustrated as two pink lobes. The circulatory system is represented by a red tube extending from the thyroid gland, containing yellow circles labeled \"T4\" and \"T3.\" The liver is situated below the circulatory system, appearing as a brown structure with a green circle labeled \"Conjugated T4 and T3.\" At the bottom of the diagram is the intestine, shown as a pink tube. A dashed blue line with a minus sign extends from the hypothalamus to the anterior pituitary gland, while solid black lines connect the anterior pituitary to the thyroid gland and the thyroid gland back to the anterior pituitary. The stimulatory pathway is indicated by plus signs next to the relevant arrows, and the inhibitory pathway by a minus sign on the dashed line. The legend, located in the bottom right corner, explains the plus and minus signs as stimulatory and inhibitory pathways, respectively." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
