<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p2_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram presents a side view of a human body from the head down to the waist, with labels pointing to various endocrine glands. The parathyroid gland is shown behind the thyroid gland, close to the trachea. The thyroid gland is located in the neck, below the larynx. The thymus gland is depicted in the upper chest area, above the heart. The ovary is located in the lower abdomen, on the left side, while the testis is on the right side. Each label is connected by a leader line or arrow pointing to the corresponding anatomical structure within the body. The diagram includes a simplified representation of internal organs and glands, with no additional details such as blood vessels or muscles." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
