<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p25_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with a blood region on the left, featuring a yellow circle labeled \"iodide porter\" with an arrow pointing towards the follicular cell. The main part of the image is a pink region representing the follicular cell. At the top of this cell, a \"tight junction\" connects two parts. Inside the follicular cell, there are several labeled components: a green circle for \"ribosomes,\" a yellow circle for \"iodide porter,\" a green circle for \"secretory vesicles with thyroglobulin precursor,\" and various arrows indicating processes such as \"H2O2,\" \"deiodination DIT & MIT,\" \"proteolysis,\" \"export,\" \"lysosomes,\" \"colloid vesicles,\" and \"endocytosis by pseudopodia.\" At the top right, a green box labeled \"thyroglobulin\" is shown with chemical structures \"I\" and \"OH.\" Near the bottom of the follicular cell, \"T3 & T4\" is labeled, and \"lumen\" is written at the bottom right corner." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/41003e33b78a> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#hasDeviation> <http://snomed.info/id/1250004> <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/d7c0b17fa043> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#about> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/10565> <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/953272c03615> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://snomed.info/id/40930008> <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p21_b1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
<http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/5499> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "hydrogen peroxide" <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/ca3f8ef9e762> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/assert/3f80480eebad> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#ClinicalAssertion> <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p47_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with a yellow-labeled \"Cytoplasm\" surrounding a purple \"Nucleus.\" Red circles labeled \"T3\" and \"T4\" are positioned outside the cell membrane on the left side. Inside the nucleus, two green hexagons labeled \"RXR\" and \"TR\" represent the retinoid X receptor and thyroid hormone receptor, respectively, with a red hexagon labeled \"CoR\" situated above them. Arrows guide the viewer: an arrow labeled \"1\" points from the \"T3\" circle to the green hexagons, indicating T3's binding to the TR. Another arrow labeled \"2\" connects \"CoR\" to the green hexagons, showing CoR's interaction with the TR-RXR complex. Arrow \"3\" extends from the green hexagons to a blue rectangle representing the DNA region with a white line for the TRE, signifying the complex binding to the TRE. Finally, arrow \"4\" leads downward from the DNA region to \"Gene expression,\" illustrating the regulation of gene transcription. Two orange squares are positioned on the right side of the DNA region, likely representing genes." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p23_b1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#FigureImage> <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
<http://snomed.info/id/50552001> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#secretes> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/1311287> <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p43_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The flowchart is organized with \"Thyroid secretion\" positioned on the left side, directing an arrow towards the central box labeled \"Free T4\". From \"Free T4\", an arrow ascends to \"Protein-bound T4\" and another branches right into four distinct pathways: feedback control, tissue action, hormone metabolism, and fecal excretion. The \"Protein-bound T4\" box is large and occupies most of the lower section of the image, with the text \"(99.96%)\" placed to its right." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
<http://example.org/medkg/inst/07452498fe10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/RXNORM/10579> <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
