<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p20_b5> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The image presents a molecular structure with two green circles labeled \"I\" positioned symmetrically on either side of a central hexagonal benzene ring. Below this benzene ring, another similar benzene ring is connected by a single bond. Extending from the bottom of the second benzene ring is a linear chain of atoms: a hydrogen atom (H) is connected to a carbon atom (C), which is bonded to an oxygen atom (O), then to another carbon atom (C), and finally to an amino group (NH2). The benzene rings are stacked vertically, and the green circles with \"I\" are placed on either side of the first benzene ring." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
