<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p51_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with a pinkish-purple capillary on the left, containing small circular blood cells. A blue, elongated structure labeled \"Thyroglobulin\" is positioned near the Golgi apparatus and Rough ER, indicated by leader lines showing their involvement in synthesis. The follicle lumen features a yellow, wavy structure labeled \"Colloid,\" connected to the thyroglobulin by leader lines. Iodide ions (I⁻) are shown moving from the capillary into the follicle lumen, with leader lines depicting their uptake and oxidation. The iodinated tyrosines, forming DIT and MIT, are linked to create T3 and T4, represented as brown and blue structures within the follicle lumen. Lysosomal processing is indicated by leader lines showing thyroglobulin colloid being endocytosed and combined with yellow, round lysosomes. The Golgi apparatus is green and granular, the Rough ER is blue and ribbed, and lysosomes are yellow and round, containing T3 and T4. Leader lines guide the movement of T3 and T4 from the follicle cell to peripheral tissues." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
