<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p14_b1> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "The diagram is organized with the Iodide pool (ECF) at the top-center, connected by an arrow to the GI tract on the right. The GI tract is positioned above the Tissues, which are situated below it. The Hormone pool (T₃ + T₄) is located at the bottom-center, receiving inputs from both the Tissues and the Thyroid pool. The Thyroid pool is on the left side, while Urination is shown at the bottom-left and Feces at the bottom-right. Curved arrows indicate the direction of iodine flow between these components." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
