<http://example.org/medkg/inst/fig/p17_b3> <http://example.org/medkg/ont#visualDescription> "A long, red, wavy line represents thyroglobulin in the leftmost panel, with two gray hexagons symbolizing tyrosine within it. The text \"thyroglobulin\" is positioned at the top-left corner, pointing to the wavy line, while \"tyrosine\" is at the bottom-left, indicating the hexagons. In the middle panel, a blue arrow labeled \"Thyroid peroxidase\" connects the left panel to the middle one, where the thyroglobulin structure now includes two green iodine atoms attached to the gray hexagons, signifying diiodotyrosine. The label \"diiodotyrosine\" is at the bottom-center, pointing to these iodine-containing hexagons. The rightmost panel is linked by another blue arrow labeled \"Thyroid peroxidase\" from the middle panel, showing a single gray hexagon with two iodine atoms, representing thyroxine. The label \"thyroxine\" is at the bottom-right, pointing to this structure." <urn:graph:thyroid_source> .
